{"title":"Career Roadmap · Zoologist","role":"Zoologist","summary":"A Zoologist studies animals, their biology, behaviour, physiology, ecology, evolution, genetics, populations and interactions with ecosystems. Zoologists can work in research institutions, universities, wildlife and biodiversity organizations, conservation programs, zoos, museums, environmental consultancies, laboratories and government agencies.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science - General / Honours)","Course":"Zoology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Zoologist studies animals, their biology, behaviour, physiology, ecology, evolution, genetics, populations and interactions with ecosystems. Zoologists can work in research institutions, universities, wildlife and biodiversity organizations, conservation programs, zoos, museums, environmental consultancies, laboratories and government agencies."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest career positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Zoology","Animal Biology","Ecology","Field Research","Statistics","GIS","Biodiversity Conservation","Scientific Communication"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc Zoology provides the foundation, but advanced research and specialist zoology roles commonly benefit from an M.Sc and, for independent research/academic careers, often a PhD."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Zoology","Animal Biology + Ecology + Evolution","Taxonomy + Physiology + Genetics","Field Biology + Laboratory Techniques","Statistics + Research Methodology","GIS + Biodiversity Data","Research / Conservation Internship","Research Assistant / Zoology Trainee","Zoologist / Wildlife Biologist / Ecologist","Specialist","Senior Researcher / Conservation Scientist","Research Lead / Principal Scientist / Academic"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","h