:"+"},{"type":"p","text":"R"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"GIS / QGIS"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Remote Sensing"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Scientific Writing"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"One Specialist Area"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Research / Field Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Identify major animal groups"},{"text":"Understand animal anatomy and physiology"},{"text":"Explain evolutionary processes"},{"text":"Understand population and community ecology"},{"text":"Conduct basic biodiversity surveys"},{"text":"Apply field sampling methods"},{"text":"Maintain structured field records"},{"text":"Analyze ecological data"},{"text":"Use basic R for statistical analysis"},{"text":"Use QGIS for spatial analysis"},{"text":"Understand wildlife monitoring methods"},{"text":"Perform basic laboratory procedures"},{"text":"Understand molecular biology techniques"},{"text":"Read scientific literature"},{"text":"Prepare scientific reports"},{"text":"Present research findings"},{"text":"Complete a research-oriented project"},{"text":"Gain practical field/laboratory internship experience"},{"text":"Select a clear zoology specialization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"A generic B.Sc Zoology profile is relatively broad. The student becomes considerably more competitive by combining zoology with field research, quantitative analysis and spatial technology."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest modern positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Zoology","Ecology/Wildlife Biology","Field Research","Statistics/R","GIS","Biodiversity Conservation","Scientific Communication"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For a laboratory-oriented student, the alternative is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Zoology","Molecular Biology","Genetics"